---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="Read our privacy policy. Fall Asleep is completely private, local-only, and tracks absolutely no user data.">
  <main class="page-container">
    <header class="page-header">
      <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Home</a>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="page-content">
      <p><strong>Effective Date:</strong> July 2026</p>
      <p>At Fall Asleep, your privacy is our absolute highest priority. We have designed this application to be entirely self-contained and local to your device.</p>
      
      <h2>1. Local Data Storage</h2>
      <p>Any personal reflections you generate while using Fall Asleep (such as your journal entries, sleep ratings, and custom preferences) are stored <strong>strictly locally</strong> in your web browser using standard client-side storage technologies (localStorage). This data never leaves your device and is never transmitted to our servers or stored in any remote database.</p>

      <h2>2. Third-Party Advertising and Cookies</h2>
      <p>We partner with Google AdSense to serve advertisements when you visit our website. Google and its partner advertising networks use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this website or other sites on the internet.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads based on your visit to Fall Asleep and other websites across the web.</li>
        <li>Users may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a> or by visiting <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AboutAds.info</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Web Analytics</h2>
      <p>We may use aggregated, non-personally identifiable web analytics (such as Google Analytics) to understand overall traffic patterns, page load performance, and popular content. These tools collect anonymous technical data such as browser type, device category, referring URL, and approximate geographic region. No personally identifiable information or personal journal text is ever linked to these metrics.</p>

      <h2>4. Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>If we make any adjustments to our privacy practices or legal disclosures, we will update the effective date on this page. Our core architectural commitment to keeping your personal thoughts and sleep logs 100% local on your own device remains absolute.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

